# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 serving window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of serving/tp4-s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled
# in by whoever drives the window; every other value is final. ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image and its stop rule.
# An EVIDENCE job: one harness on card M alone (C2_CARDS=pair: cardm is a pair-shaped step; the quad jobs reset all four boards, this
# one never does). The harness runs its own pinned image and mounts this checkout's scripts as the code under test. The K64j graft
# binary is pinned by EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256: read the launched argv, a graft mounted is not a graft executed. Placeholders:
# @K64J_GRAFT_DIR@ (the graft directory of the K64j build) and @K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256@ (packed_any_admission.K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256).
# NEEDS the four-card harness ports of the serving branch (E1: k64j_card_b.py --kv-heads 1; E2: the four-card extent reader,
# K64J_HARNESS=extent_reader TP4_WIDTH=4): a run on a harness without them refuses its flags.
# EV-W2: the four-card extent reader twin (extent_attention_replay_tp.py) through ChipView(chips=4), reduced scope (seed 0), under
# the watcher. IMAGE is the image the four-card reader's pinned siblings (the mask and fold modules) are served from:
# @SERVED_IMAGE@ is tp4-stackfix-3's reference in the rig daemon. A watcher pass (scope=reduced) is never CB2b's evidence.
# Duration (estimate): 4-8 min. Stop rule: any differing decisive comparison stops S2 TP4.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stackfix-3
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections R1,S,R2,R4 --seeds 0 --variants normal
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=extent_reader TP4_WIDTH=4 WATCHER=1 IMAGE=@SERVED_IMAGE@ KOPGRAFT64=@K64J_GRAFT_DIR@ EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=@K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256@
